sash-rt licensing
=================

The project-authored runtime code in sash-rt is licensed under the GNU
General Public License, version 3 only, with the additional permissions
of the GCC Runtime Library Exception, version 3.1.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only WITH GCC-exception-3.1

The full license texts are in:

  ../LICENSE          GNU General Public License, version 3
  ../COPYING.RUNTIME  GCC Runtime Library Exception, version 3.1

The exception applies to project-authored code and modifications in the
Rust, C and assembly sources used to build the sash-rt runtime library.
It does not apply to the sash compiler or standalone tools.

Subject to the exception's terms, independent programs linked with this
runtime may be distributed under licenses of their authors' choice.
The exception does not make the runtime itself permissively licensed:
distribution of the runtime on its own remains subject to GPLv3.

Third-party material
--------------------

Third-party portions retain their existing copyright notices and licenses.
Neither the project license nor the runtime exception replaces those terms.
In particular:

  - The Plan 9-derived regex sources in csrc/ are accompanied by
    ../contrib/plan9port-regexp/LICENSE.
  - The original FreeRTOS allocator notice in csrc/heap4.c is retained;
    its upstream license is in ../contrib/freertos-heap4/LICENSE.md.
  - Rust dependencies and other linked third-party components retain
    their respective licenses.

Retain the third-party notices when distributing copies or compiled
programs incorporating that material, as required by those licenses.

There is no warranty, to the extent permitted by applicable law.
See GPLv3 sections 15-17 for the warranty and liability terms.
